   "daf": "33a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "וְאֵין חוֹתְכִין אוֹתוֹ, בֵּין בְּדָבָר שֶׁהוּא מִשּׁוּם שְׁבוּת וּבֵין בְּדָבָר שֶׁהוּא מִשּׁוּם לֹא תַעֲשֶׂה. מִשּׁוּם שְׁבוּת — מַגָּלָא. לֹא תַעֲשֶׂה — סַכִּינָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna stated: «One may not cut» the shofar if it needs to be prepared, «neither with an object that is prohibited due to a rabbinic decree nor with an object» that may not be used «due to» a Torah «prohibition.» The Gemara explains: An example of an object prohibited «due to a rabbinic decree» is «a sickle,» which is not ordinarily used for preparing a shofar; an example of an object that may not be used due to «a prohibition» by Torah law is «a knife.»"
  }
